Advanced project — coupled equilibria, activities, and model criticism (@gc-equilibrium-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @general-chemistry, #source "../sources/Analytical-Chemistry-Harvey.lingua#r_0XMY75E3FRXRGR3BK28V3JAC0T", #source "../sources/Chem1-Lower.lingua#r_0NFQA43WZVMECZY6SKZJMRXWBZ", #source "../sources/IUPAC-Green-Book.lingua#r_5SR8CP04E580VSV69MYQNSZ73F", #source "../sources/Henry-Law-Sander.lingua#r_4HW63C2ZE42PFRFC294FDPTYWH", #general-chemistry "A-kinetic-and-thermal-investigation.lingua#r_71VHHPY63F3DGW1PJ5K8HDSYQB") { r_6GQB2QBSJ0BJ4YYVNCAP1AF0V6
**Read:** [Analytical Chemistry 2.1 — David Harvey](../sources/Analytical-Chemistry-Harvey.lingua#r_0XMY75E3FRXRGR3BK28V3JAC0T), chapter 6 completely and the selected analytical context; [Chem1 General Chemistry Virtual Textbook — Stephen Lower](../sources/Chem1-Lower.lingua#r_0NFQA43WZVMECZY6SKZJMRXWBZ), the full advanced acid/base, carbonate, and exact-solution lessons; [Quantities, Units and Symbols in Physical Chemistry — IUPAC Green Book](../sources/IUPAC-Green-Book.lingua#r_5SR8CP04E580VSV69MYQNSZ73F), the complete abridged volume during advanced study; [Compilation of Henry’s law constants, version 5.0.0 — Rolf Sander](../sources/Henry-Law-Sander.lingua#r_4HW63C2ZE42PFRFC294FDPTYWH), the relevant definitions and original sources for a gas-coupled case.

Choose a chemical system connecting at least several of acid/base, complexation, precipitation, gas partition, and a defined water/mineral question. Begin with the original monoprotic titration model as a numerical benchmark, then derive the new species, reactions, balances, phase/open-boundary constraints, and activity assumptions from the actual question.

Read Harvey's complete equilibrium chapter, the assigned Chem1 exact-calculation and application units, the relevant Green Book definitions, and primary/evaluated sources for every needed constant. Identify convention, medium, temperature, phase, uncertainty, and source history. A table of apparently compatible numbers can conceal different standard states or conditional constants.

Develop analytic limits and simpler independent cases before solving the full system. Check nonnegativity, charge/component closure, phase consistency, equations, and numerical tolerance. Compare an ideal model with a justified nonideal alternative, identify valid ranges, and examine sensitivity and parameter identifiability. A numerical root does not establish that all chemically important species were included.

**Produce:** derivation, documented inputs/constants, a reproducible implementation, independent validation, distribution/response plots, uncertainty/model-sensitivity discussion, and an interpreted chemical result. Compare closed and open boundaries where meaningful. Explain which observations could test or distinguish the competing models.

Have another reader reconstruct the small benchmarks and a substantial case, or document a bounded self-restoration if independent access is unavailable. Preserve criticism and a substantive revision. Use the shared computational and metrology Records rather than repeating their entire method here. The outcome should support a detailed technical discussion of assumptions and failure conditions, not merely a colorful speciation diagram.

**Continue:** [Advanced project — infer a kinetic model from chemical and measurement evidence](A-kinetic-and-thermal-investigation.lingua#r_71VHHPY63F3DGW1PJ5K8HDSYQB).

